    {
      "title": "Activist wins 10-year fight against homophobic Trinidad and Tobago laws",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/activist-jason-jones-wins-10-year-fight-against-homophobic-trinidad-tobago-laws",
      "description": "<p>Jason Jones welcomes decision by privy council in London to overturn 2025 ruling that outlawed anal sex</p><p>A gay man has won a historic 10-year battle against Trinidad and Tobago’s homophobic laws with a landmark UK appeals court ruling that could help overturn similar anti-gay laws in other Caribbean countries.</p><p>The privy council, based in London, overturned a 2025 decision by Trinidad and Tobago’s court of appeal that recriminalised consensual anal sex, seven years after the Trinidadian activist Jason Jones secured a high court judgment declaring the country’s colonial-era “buggery” laws unconstitutional.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/activist-jason-jones-wins-10-year-fight-against-homophobic-trinidad-tobago-laws\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-10T17:55:10"
    }
